   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the state finance law, in relation to establishing the state university of New York and the city university of New York endowment fund",
    "basePrintNo": "S8066",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8066-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §92-gg, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "State Finance Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S8066\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the state finance law, in relation to establishing the\nstate university of New York and the city university of New York\nendowment fund\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to create an endowment fund for both the\nstate university of New York and the city university of New York with\nfunds being held and invested by the comptroller.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Amends the state finance law be adding section 92-gg which\nestablishes the state university of New York endowment fund and the\ncity university of New York endowment fund which will be in the\ncustody of the comptroller. The assets and income held within the\nfunds will be held and invested by the comptroller as the trustee.\nThe state university of New York endowment fund and the city\nuniversity of New York endowment fund will be made up of any funds\nthat are transferred to these endowments as well as any other deposits\nmade from other public or private sources. Also, ten percent of money\nreceived from settlements or judgments in claims or causes of actions\nby the state or any agency will be transferred to the comptroller\nwhere it will in turn be transferred to the endowment funds. Funds\nthat are transferred to these endowment funds are solely for use by\nthe state university of New York and the city university of New York.\nThese funds are also only in place to supplement rather than supplant\nfunds provided by the state. Annual payments from the investment\nearnings of the endowments will be used as determined by the board of\ntrustees and may be spent on, but not limited to, areas such as\nemployment of additional full-time faculty members, student financial\naid, grants for research and development and other such higher\neducation purposes.\n\nSection 2. Establishes the effective date of this law.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nFor too long, our public higher education systems have suffered cuts\nin the amount of resources provided by the state. This lack of funds,\nalong with growing enrollment, has caused more adjunct faculty to be\nhired instead of full time faculty. Both SUNY and CUNY have lamented\nthe fact that their fiscal status prevents replacing adjunct faculty\nwith full time faculty at a faster rate. It is thought that additional\nfunds from the endowment could assist the systems in this regard.\n\nAn active endowment fund encourages contributions from alumni, faculty\nand philanthropists. It demonstrates the regard that the State and the\ncommunity have for our public higher education systems. The funds will\nalso provide much needed resources for faculty, student aid and\nresearch and development.\n\nThe funding mechanism for the endowment does not require taxpayer\nfunds. It uses a portion of any settlements from judgements arising\nfrom any claim or cause of action brought by the state. In this way we\ncontinue to build our intellectual capital in this state.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nTo be determined\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act will take effect immediately.\n",
